course: dictionary
lesson: 14273
title: Nodding and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nodding means moving your head up and down. You nod to say yes, to agree, or to show you are listening. «Ben nodded when Mrs Khan asked if he understood.» The nod shows yes without any words.
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so read the clues around it. «Nadia was nodding off during the film.» Nodding off means falling asleep by accident, because her head drops and her eyes close.
explain: Nodding can also be part of a phrase. «Ella has only a nodding acquaintance with her new neighbour.» A nodding acquaintance means you know someone only a little. Ella is not nodding at her neighbour here, so check the whole sentence.
explain: Nodding can describe flowers too. «The nodding daffodils bent their heads in the spring breeze.» Nodding means hanging down here. Swap in your meaning to check: "the hanging daffodils bent their heads" still makes sense.
fact: Nodding is a form of the verb nod: nod, nods, nodded, nodding.
fact: «Nodding» can also be an adjective, as in «a nodding flower».
fact: «Nodding off» means falling asleep, often by accident.
fact: «Nodding along» means agreeing or joining in as someone talks.
fact: In Bulgaria, a nod can mean no, so body language can change from country to country.
exercise: «Sam nodded when the teacher asked if he was ready.» What does the nod show? | No, I am lost | I am going to sleep | I am hungry | *Yes, or I agree
exercise: «Grandpa was nodding off in his chair after lunch.» What does nodding off mean? | Waving to someone | Standing up quickly | *Falling asleep, often by accident | Eating a big dinner
exercise: «The flowers were nodding in the breeze.» What does nodding mean here? | Singing loudly | Shining brightly | Growing very tall | *Hanging their heads down
test: «Ana and I have only a nodding acquaintance; we say hello at the bus stop.» What does a nodding acquaintance mean? | Your best friend | A stranger you dislike | *Someone you know only a little | A person who sings with you
test: In Bulgaria a nod can mean no. What does this show? | Nodding always means yes everywhere | Nodding is a kind of sport | Bulgarians cannot nod | *Body language can change from country to country
exam: «The class were nodding along as Priya explained the sum.» What does nodding along mean? | Falling asleep | Hanging their heads down | Shouting at the teacher | *Agreeing or joining in as someone talks
